# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in.
# Crypto needs NO key at all — the browser calls keyless Binance endpoints directly.

# Which source the /stocks pages read. LEAVE THIS AS fixture ON ANY DEPLOYED URL.
#
#   fixture (default, and the value used when this var is unset or misspelled)
#           serves lib/stocks-fixture.ts — a fully synthetic dataset of invented tickers
#           and invented prices. Safe to publish.
#   live    calls Massive.com. LOCAL / PRIVATE USE ONLY.
#
# Why: Massive's Market Data terms grant personal, non-business use only (§1, which also
# bars using the data "to build an application intended for use by end users other than
# you"), and §5(c) prohibits *displaying* the data or anything derived from it "including
# charts". A public demo is an application for other end users, so it may not show their
# numbers — and a frozen snapshot would not help, because a captured session is still their
# Market Data. Paid individual plans do not change this; only a Business plan permits
# public display. There is also no attribution requirement: a "Powered by Massive" credit
# would itself breach §6's trademark clause, so do not add one.
#
# The gate fails safe: only the exact token "live" reaches the upstream, and having
# MASSIVE_API_KEY set is deliberately NOT enough on its own.
STOCKS_DATA_MODE=fixture

# Massive.com (ex-Polygon.io) US-equities data. Only read when STOCKS_DATA_MODE=live.
# SERVER-ONLY: never rename this to NEXT_PUBLIC_*. Without it the stocks routes answer
# 503 {error:'no-key'} in live mode, and every crypto page keeps working regardless.
MASSIVE_API_KEY=
